transducer/gauresh/classloader/
Has the complete code.

transducer/gauresh/classloader/global-env/ 
	package  that sets up the PDV server

transducer/gauresh/classloader/testclasses/
	package that has sample transducer code

transducer/gauresh/classloader/transducer-loader/
	contains main policy file...
	contains packages that provide environment for the transducer..
	These are the packages that involve actual environment code
	edu.ucla.cens.pdc.transducer.loader.Javarunner.java - contains main that sets off the environment
	edu.ucla.cens.pdc.transducer.loader.datastructures.StreamData.java -  Class that provides access for transducers to data streams
	transducer have to import this package

transducer/gauresh/classloader/transducer-secman/
	contains packages that implement the security manager

Running the program

1. You should have ccnx compiled and installed. Go to the bin directory and run ccndstart script. Also install google protobuffers.
2. CLASSPATH should have  ccnx.jar, mongo.jar, protobuf.jar, and the classfiles in the classloader class. you would find them in libpdc
3. go to transducers/gauresh/classloader/src and  run
	java -Djava.security.policy=../allPolicy.policy edu.ucla.cens.pdc.transducer.loader.JavaRunner ./edu/ucla/cens/pdc/transducer/loader/config1.xml
4. The config1.xml is the config file that is read to figure out how the transducers are oranized and there input and output


